/// <remarks>
///  <para>
///   Recording is started by <see cref="StartRecording"/> and stopped by <see cref="StopRecording"/>. The screen is
///   captured at a low frame rate until recording is stopped. Identical frames are coalesced, keeping the number of
///   recorded frames and the resulting file size small. A checksum of every captured row is computed with
///   <see cref="Crc32"/> and only the rows that change are actually written to the animation, allowing for much
///   smaller files for the common case where only a portion of the screen is in motion.
///  </para>
